I am an Associate Professor in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering of University of Virginia. I am also a member of the UVA [https://engineering.virginia.edu/link-lab Link Lab], and an active faculty in the [https://engineering.virginia.edu/offices-programs/computer-engineering-program/academics/cpe-graduate-programs Computer Engineering program]. I got my B.S. and M.S. from Tsinghua University, and Ph.D. from UCLA. I received the NSF CAREER award in 2022.

My research interests span a number of interdisciplinary topics in AI/ML and its engineering applications. Some of my current research topics are:
- In-context learning and Transformers
- Reinforcement learning and multi-armed bandits
- Distributed and decentralized learning
- AI/ML for wireless

#{{<font color = DarkOrange size=+1.0><b>}} Prospective Students: {{</b></font>}} Working with talented graduate students has been one of the most pleasant experiences in my faculty career, and I am always looking for candidates with strong mathematical background and/or interest in practical systems. Feel free to contact me with your CV and transcripts.
#*Prospective Students:* One  fully-funded PhD student position starting Fall 2021 is currently available. Candidates with strong mathematical background and interest in machine learning and/or wireless communications are encouraged to contact me with your CV and transcripts.

#{{<font color = DarkOrange size=+1.0><b>}} Prospective students: {{</b></font>}} *Two (2) PhD student positions* and *one (1) jointly advised PhD student position* are currently available in my group. Starting date is Fall 2024 or Spring 2025. I am also looking for a strong *post-doc* to join my group. Please feel free to contact me with your CV and transcripts.

#{{<font color = DarkOrange size=+1.0><b>}} Postdoc position available: {{</b></font>}}  I am looking for a postdoc in my group. Candidates with strong mathematical background and/or interest in practical systems are welcome to contact me with your CV.


== News
- Aug. 2026: Area Chair for ICLR 2026. Senior Program Committee for AAAI 2027. 
- Aug. 2026: TPC co-chair of the [https://icc2027.ieee-icc.org/ Communication Theory Symposium at IEEE International Conference on Communications (ICC) 2027].
- Aug. 2026: PhD student [https://chenyewang-ee.github.io/ Chenye Wang] joins our [group.html group]. Welcome!
- June 2026: Action Editor for [https://jmlr.org/tmlr/ Transactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR)]. Associate Editor for [https://www.nature.com/npjwireltech Springer Nature npj Wireless Technology].
- Apr. 2026: Lead organizer for the [https://ai4nextg.github.io/ Second AI4NextG Workshop @ ICML 2026] in Seoul, South Korea. The focus is on academia-industry collaborations. Please consider submitting your work!
- Apr. 2026: PhD student [https://chen-1031.github.io/ Zihan Chen] received the 2026 Charles L. Brown Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering's Louis T Rader Graduate Research Award. Congratulations!
- Jan. 2026: Area Chair for ICML 2026.



